      "body": "## Summary\nFix sgl-project/sglang#9889.\n\nAnalyzed all three `torch.nonzero()` call sites flagged in the issue:\n\n| File | Before | Fix |\n|------|--------|-----|\n| `gemma3_mm.py:212` | `(...).cpu().nonzero()` | already on CPU — no change needed |\n| `janus_pro.py:479` | `image_token_mask.nonzero()` (on CUDA input_ids) | explicitly `.cpu()` before `.nonzero()` |\n| `phi4mm_utils.py:84` | `(...).nonzero()` (seq_range from `torch.arange` on CPU) | already on CPU — no change needed |\n\nOnly `janus_pro.py` actually forces an implicit host-device sync today.\nThe other two call sites are already CPU-resident.  Making the sync\nboundary explicit in the remaining case avoids accidental performance\nregressions in future refactors.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] Code inspection confirms janus_pro.py input_ids are CUDA tensors\n- [x] gemma3_mm.py already calls `.cpu()`\n- [x] phi4mm_utils.py seq_range is created with `torch.arange` (CPU)\n\n/cc @merrymercy\n\n---\nDCO: Signed-off-by: yancy <yancy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38411875707](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38411875707)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38411877187](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38411877187)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38411875327](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38411875327)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
