            "body": "@merrymercy @Fridge003 — Hi folks, I took a quick look at the three `torch.nonzero()` call sites from #9889. Only `janus_pro.py:479` actually forces an implicit host-device sync (the other two already call `.cpu()` or create tensors on CPU). The fix is one line: move the mask onto CPU explicitly before `.nonzero()`. Mind taking a look when you have a moment? Thanks!\n",
